# Backstage

Internal HRMS docs + operator console (`apps/backstage`, port 5001). Next.js 16 App Router. **Feature-based architecture** — interactive code lives under `features/<domain>/<capability>/`; `app/` is a thin route map. Full layout is in `apps/backstage/AGENTS.md`.

## Architecture (follow for new work)

```text
app/           thin routes only
features/      interactive capabilities — features/<domain>/<capability>/
shared/        cross-cutting (auth, db, ui, theme, resolve)
components/    docs chrome only (header, guides article UI, auth menu)
lib/           markdown/content loaders (docs, wiki, guides)
content/       on-disk markdown trees
```

```text
# ❌ BAD
features/employee-access/employee-access-screen.tsx
features/employer-settings/
lib/queries/getAccess.ts
features/roles/

# ✅ GOOD
features/employee/access/access-screen.tsx
features/employer/settings/settings-screen.tsx
features/employer/roles/roles-screen.tsx
```

- Leaf barrel `index.ts` per capability. No domain-level barrel. Import `@/features/employee/access`.
- App-wide login: `features/auth/`. Cross-cutting resolve: `shared/employee/`.
- New interactive area: add `features/<domain>/<capability>/` + thin `app/` route. Do not dump screens into `components/` or `lib/`.
- Import with `@/`. No parent-relative `../`. Same-directory `./` is allowed.
- **Docs/wiki/guides** (Tailwind + `prose`, markdown on disk) vs **operator `/features`** (antd 6 + `@hrms/db`) — do not mix stacks casually.
- Product guide markdown ≠ Features code: guides are `content/guides` → `/docs/guides`; ops capabilities are `features/` → `/features`.

## Content trees

| Folder | Served at | Edit how |
|---|---|---|
| `content/guides/<menu-folder>/<slug>.md` | `/docs/guides/<menu-folder>/<slug>` | `/document-feature` (freeze previous date first) or Admin-approved in-app proposal |
| `content/guides/<menu-folder>/<slug>/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | `/docs/guides/<menu-folder>/<slug>/YYYY-MM-DD` | Immutable snapshot — do not edit |
| `content/guides/_proposals/` | Admin queue only | In-app Edit; gitignored |
| `content/llm-wiki/**` | `/wiki/<path>` | `/sync-llm-wiki` (mirror). `/track-db-updates` may patch pages contradicted by this run's SQL delta |
| `content/wiki/database-changelog.md` | `/docs/database-changelog` | `/track-db-updates` only |
| `content/wiki/*.md` | `/docs/<slug>` | Hand-authored; wiki-sync must not touch |

Adding a `.md` file is enough. Slugs come from `readdirSync` in `lib/docs.ts`, `lib/llm-wiki.ts`, `lib/guides.ts`. Do not hardcode route lists.

## Feature guide shape

YAML may contain `confidence`, `last-analyzed`, `menu`, and optional `submenu`. `menu`/`submenu` match the HRMS left-nav; use `menu: Platform` when the feature is not in the sidebar. On disk, put the file in `content/guides/<menu-folder>/` (`Leave & Attendance` → `leave-and-attendance`). `last-analyzed` is parsed (CRLF-safe) and shown under the H1 as `Last analyzed: YYYY-MM-DD`. Put sources in a trailing `## Reference` section, not in frontmatter — leftover `---` renders as a horizontal rule.

Section order: Overview → Workflow (mermaid flowchart) → Request journey (mermaid `sequenceDiagram`, request start → end) → Entry points → call chain → API endpoints → procs/tables → Table relationships (mermaid `erDiagram`) → Known gaps → Reference.

Write standard ```` ```mermaid ```` fences. `MermaidAwarePre` renders them; no app-specific syntax.

## Code

- Docs/wiki: Tailwind 4 + `prose`. Operator `/features`: antd 6.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for theme, nav, TOC, mermaid zoom, version select, editor, proposal review, and operator interactivity.
- `params` is a `Promise` — `await params`. `generateStaticParams` on every dynamic page.
- Explicit `): React.JSX.Element`. Fresh `createSlugger()` per document (TOC ids must match heading ids).
- Import with `@/` (`@/lib/guides`, `@/components/...`, `@/features/...`). No parent-relative `../`. Same-directory `./` is allowed.

```yaml
# ❌ BAD
sources:
  - lib/guides.ts
# ✅ GOOD
---
confidence: high
last-analyzed: 2026-08-14
menu: Leave & Attendance
submenu: L&A Tasks
---
```
